    "body": "Thanks for raising this! It came out of this [Chromium bug](https://crbug.com/1063756), which has more discussion, particularly about cross-browser behavior.\r\n\r\nCan you comment on why [the hidden attribute](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-hidden-attribute) (which is global) doesn't just automatically apply to `<embed>` elements? It says\r\n\r\n> When an element has the [hidden](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-hidden) attribute in the hidden state, it indicates that the element is not yet, or is no longer, directly relevant to the page's current state, or that it is being used to declare content to be reused by other parts of the page as opposed to being directly accessed by the user. User agents should not render elements that are in the [hidden state](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-hidden-hidden-state). This requirement may be implemented indirectly through the style layer. For example, a web browser could implement these requirements [using the rules suggested in the Rendering section](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#hiddenCSS).\r\n\r\nI was just going on that when I wrote the test.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
